{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "02X8", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-2-1-categories}\n\n"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:59b6ef66b35b76d755a6e633557d7043fa8b375e01f831b4c494771f96e807e4", "source_text": "(2, 1)-categories", "source_text_hash": "sha256:96bffb88d9d578f2970e6af4a1e720934bb8aad158eac0755b45007ee7ce57d0", "unit_id": "tag:02X8:title"}
{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "02X8", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$2$", "MATH_0002": "$2$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": "\n\n"}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:30a9c1d9b4fa53bcc0a2a072b21e1b9b010a3af0ebe92482f9e839ef237579b5", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:287eac9cba3ce879ac70d8b680e0a2ca897da46ae93623dbcfe156449c0e81c4", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\nSome <MATH_0001>-categories have\nthe property that all <MATH_0002>-morphisms are isomorphisms. These will\nplay an important role in the following, and they are easier to work with.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:8861d7baaf63dafa9d9dc293edf236c89c1cd483c2108e5e563d361b0d644c3d", "unit_id": "tag:02X8:p001"}
{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "02X8", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$(2, 1)$", "MATH_0002": "$2$", "MATH_0003": "$2$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-2-1-category}\n", "suffix": "\n\\end{definition}\n\n"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:accc2b0f51dc20c705997ffa13bf1fa556113d614cac93d9bbeb0b16ef44509e", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:f75e17b13ea1a006631f5117a1570641630c5cbfebba841f238ddf57dfb60856", "source_text": "A (strict) <TEXTITOPEN_0001><MATH_0001>-category<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> is a <MATH_0002>-category in which all\n<MATH_0003>-morphisms are isomorphisms.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:bacf7e55c93dc162be39300d104c9014076e1013b55c9d91270f68a1536c95b0", "unit_id": "tag:02X8:definition"}
{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "example", "parent_tag": "02X8", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$2$", "MATH_0002": "$\\textit{Cat}$", "MATH_0003": "$(2, 1)$", "MATH_0004": "$2$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{remark-big-2-categories}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{example}\n\\label{example-2-1-category-of-categories}\n", "suffix": "\n\\end{example}\n\n"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:457a0cccd25370e0b2d60f48b308c7c2a21b9854784a72fc9b8fa8a4f51de56d", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:7582668e8cccfa69d632da00f859a489f6530337744769198dca0334656d6ca6", "source_text": "The <MATH_0001>-category <MATH_0002>, see Remark <REF_0001>,\ncan be turned into a <MATH_0003>-category by only allowing isomorphisms of\nfunctors as <MATH_0004>-morphisms.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:3ad4b452ea2da9d438732e24f9a49fe5b2adc861e0376f47c26f90c4e319895a", "unit_id": "tag:02X8:example"}
{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "02X8", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$2$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0003": "$(2, 1)$", "MATH_0004": "$2$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{C}'$", "MATH_0006": "$1$", "MATH_0007": "$2$", "MATH_0008": "$2$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0010": "$\\mathcal{C}'$", "MATH_0011": "$(2, 1)$", "MATH_0012": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0013": "$(2, 1)$", "MATH_0014": "$2$", "MATH_0015": "$1$", "MATH_0016": "$2$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "STRUCT_0002": "\\it"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": "\n\n"}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:32d030aeb6b0bda7c4d269d8a4175527b58c34f4a4d6aed41b40f2078ae951e7", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:3bde80663c5f7d229dc7dd9a77d9dcf8096029235e38b5810c4ce0eaf3f7700c", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\nIn fact, more generally any <MATH_0001>-category\n<MATH_0002> produces a <MATH_0003>-category by considering the sub <MATH_0004>-category\n<MATH_0005> with the same objects and <MATH_0006>-morphisms but whose\n<MATH_0007>-morphisms are the invertible <MATH_0008>-morphisms of <MATH_0009>.\nIn this situation we will say ``{<STRUCT_0002> let <MATH_0010> be\nthe <MATH_0011>-category associated to <MATH_0012>}'' or similar.\nFor example, the <MATH_0013>-category of groupoids means the\n<MATH_0014>-category whose objects are groupoids, whose\n<MATH_0015>-morphisms are functors and whose <MATH_0016>-morphisms are\nisomorphisms of functors. Except that this is a bad example as a\ntransformation between functors between groupoids is automatically\nan isomorphism!", "source_text_hash": "sha256:a8ff7d9b990ba52f45568bee65aa63f3136e9c1440b930ac4036e3b2bb97710b", "unit_id": "tag:02X8:p002"}
{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "remark", "parent_tag": "02X8", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$2$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{example-2-1-category-of-categories}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{remark}\n\\label{remark-other-2-categories}\n", "suffix": "\n\\end{remark}\n\n"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:b15315ec3c2fa7b154c0d17c24b63d47f12b572ea3fa602a460510e1a685b882", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:fdcb8058f21a7384fb6adc19f3ace25f6d02d22aa0475f338b0d47e83c3e0306", "source_text": "Thus there are variants of the construction of\nExample <REF_0001>\nabove where we look at the <MATH_0001>-category of groupoids,\nor categories fibred in groupoids over a fixed\ncategory, or stacks. And so on.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:521aadf0e7caea1937e9d8b0395c68058bd01d30cc2f80e37cb4d6107e3627b9", "unit_id": "tag:02X8:remark"}
